## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of basic synchronization primitives, correctness under contention, and memory ordering pitfalls in a beginner-friendly yet non-trivial way.

## Key Concepts
- Atomic operations and memory orders
- FIFO fairness and blocking behavior
- Spinlock design trade-offs and wrap-around handling
- Basic micro-benchmarking considerations under contention

## Code Example
```javascript
#include <stdatomic.h>
#include <stdint.h>

typedef struct {
  atomic_uint64_t next_ticket;
  atomic_uint64_t now_serving;
} ticket_lock_t;

void ticket_lock_acquire(ticket_lock_t *lock) {
  uint64_t my = atomic_fetch_add_explicit(&lock->next_ticket, 1, memory_order_relaxed);
  while (atomic_load_explicit(&lock->now_serving, memory_order_acquire) != my) {
    // busy-wait
  }
}

void ticket_lock_release(ticket_lock_t *lock) {
  atomic_fetch_add_explicit(&lock->now_serving, 1, memory_order_release);
}
```

